## Context

Rung 3 of the ladder (`plugins/sdt-sitter/TESTING.md`, ruling 2026-09-23). The
author folded lifecycle testing into this rung rather than keeping it as a
layer, and merged "full Menagerie" with "wild documents": the corpus is where
the wild beasts belong. It is not to be called "acceptance": acceptance is the
author's own use (rung 5).

Split by the raid of 2026-09-23 (Imagine pass): as one ticket it bundled four
failure surfaces — scale, three lifecycle mechanisms, a completeness assertion,
a rename — so a failure two hours into a 114-document run would not say which
change broke it. The ruling fixes the *shipped test*: one scenario, one rung. The
children converge on that one script; this tracker holds the one recorded run.

## Children

- 0820 — rename the driver and its records away from "acceptance" (first)
- 0821 — the whole Menagerie, every attachment a pack or a named reason
- 0822 — lifecycle in the scenario: replace, disable and re-enable, restart

## Exit criteria

A recorded pass on the whole Menagerie with the integrity check (0816) green,
exercising the lifecycle steps in the one converged script. Once 0794 lands,
the pass includes its two documents. Integration review per the tracker rule.
